  "scene": {
    "id": "check-pilot3",
    "language": "[0]Okay. So, I'm gonna be explaining sort of the check situation. Um, when this sort of takes place is when a, uh, teammate has the ball either on the halfway line or they're bringing the ball out of the defense, so this will either be my central midfielder or my center back bringing the ball out of defense. Um, and I will be trying to make a passing option for them to sort of, you know, give them a place to relieve the pressure that's on them. Um, so, uh, when I start the simulation, I'm gonna run into space, um, and depending on what my opponent does, I will then make a decision. Um, so, I'm gonna try maybe get a little bit further away from my teammate, maybe open up the pitch a bit, um, and when I start this, I'm gonna see how my defender follows me. If he follows me very closely, I might try to lose him, um, by, you know, moving, um, the opposite direction of his momentum to unsettle him, or if I feel like, you know, he's, um, not, um, unbalanced enough to do that, I might just play the safe option and give it back to my teammate. Alternatively, if he doesn't move at all, if he just stays where he is, I'll turn and face the goal. Um, so, (sighs) I'm gonna start the situation, make some space, my teammate[1] gives it to me. [2]At this point, it's all about checking over your shoulder, looking over your shoulder to see where the, where the defender is. Um, I can see he's right here. I've got lots of space on my left-hand side. I might receive the ball [3]and turn this way. Lots and lots of open space to either take a shot, to pass, to cross, and in this case, I'm gonna choose to shoot.[4] Um, and then there we go. There's a goal, and happy days. Uh-",
